{
  "_doc": "Two-axis reconciliation for clinical-research OOUX objects — enforced by tools/lint_layering.py. See docs/ooux-layer-blindness.md. AXIS 1 KIND (Jessica Talisman): is this a class (an object / the TBox, which is small) or a property/relation/context (the ABox, where the data lives)? A property reified as a class is demoted, not tiered. AXIS 2 TIER (only for kind=class): which layer owns it — dedupe/subclass (resolved) vs promote/review (backlog). dedupe/subclass PASS; kind!=class, promote, and review WARN (tracked) until --strict. An object absent from this map is an untriaged shadow/orphan and FAILS the gate — that is what prevents recurrence.",
  "_kinds": {
    "class": "an object / a TBox class — proceed to the TIER axis",
    "property": "an attribute or a literal value (firstName, date, a metric) — model as a property with a domain, not a class",
    "relation": "a relationship, role, or CONTEXT (Jessica Talisman: 'context is a property, not an object') — model as an object property, not a class"
  },
  "_verdicts": {
    "dedupe": "same concept the parent already owns — bind the view/target to it, do not re-mint",
    "subclass": "domain-native specialization — mint in cr:, but rdfs:subClassOf the named parent",
    "promote": "cross-domain primitive; no parent exists yet — candidate for Core or a mid-layer (RFC)",
    "review": "home tier not yet decided — tracked so the map stays complete; resolve before federation",
    "demote": "not a class at all — a property/relation/context reified as an object (KIND axis); re-model as a property",
    "defer": "out of this domain's scope — a different bucket owns it (e.g. a finance bucket); re-enters when that bucket forms"
  },
